      "problem": "What is the missing number in the following equality?\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\times 3\\,\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{12}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $3\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{(3\\times 3)+2}{3}=\\frac{11}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\times \\frac{11}{3}=\\frac{1\\times 11}{4\\times 3}=\\frac{11}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $11.$",
